  {
   "id": "C35",
   "adr": "ADR-0019",
   "where": "design/gdd/player-controller-input.md",
   "old": "through four published **Class B mutators**",
   "new": "through four published status-returning mutators (Class A in ADR-0003's taxonomy: each has a `check_*` twin and returns OK, REFUSED or -fault_code; ADR-0019 § 2.5)"
  },
  {
   "id": "C36",
   "adr": "ADR-0019",
   "where": "design/gdd/player-controller-input.md",
   "old": "**→ ADR** (InputMap vs a custom binding layer; edge detection by event vs polling).",
   "new": "**Decided in ADR-0019 § 3.2 and § 3.3**: `InputMap` actions registered at runtime from data with a non-zero engine deadzone, the any-device wildcard and `physical_keycode`; ordered edges latched in `_input` (key, mouse-button and pad-button events only; pad-axis motion is continuous) and continuous state polled in `_process`; devices identified by event type."
  },
  {
   "id": "C37",
   "adr": "ADR-0019",
   "where": "design/gdd/player-controller-input.md",
   "old": "the engine's echo flag is **[UNV]** until the ADR spike",
   "new": "probed 2026-10-29 on 4.7.2: a synthetic echo event does not re-fire `is_action_just_pressed`; real OS key repeat is still **[UNV]** until PC-INPUT-SPIKE-1 (d), a RECORDED item with a held-set fallback"
  },
  {
   "id": "C38",
   "adr": "ADR-0019",
   "where": "design/gdd/player-controller-input.md",
   "old": "THEN** the Suit read it requests is `locomotion_cap` only and never Suit's internal vitals ladder.",
   "new": "THEN** the Suit reads it requests are `locomotion_cap` and `stowed_heavy` only (TR-suit-033) and never Suit's internal vitals ladder."
  },
  {
   "id": "C39",
   "adr": "ADR-0019",
   "where": "design/gdd/player-controller-input.md",
   "old": "Derived (idle breathing, tick-stepped) *(Amended 2026-10-27 — re-review)*: `frame_idle = posmod(floor((T − T_enter) / IDLE_FRAME_TICKS), 6)`",
   "new": "Derived (idle breathing, tick-stepped) *(Amended 2026-10-27 — re-review; free-running from the committed tick, ADR-0019 § 7.1)*: `frame_idle = posmod(floor(T / IDLE_FRAME_TICKS), 6)`"
  },
  {
   "id": "C40",
   "adr": "ADR-0019",
   "where": "design/gdd/player-controller-input.md",
   "old": "Either the Adapter hands the cursor position and zoom edges to the pipeline root, or the lint carries an allow-list naming the pipeline root.",
   "new": "Resolved by ADR-0019 § 6.4 and § 8.1: the Adapter owns every Input read, the pipeline root reads none, zoom edges reach it by `request_zoom_step` and the cursor is published as `AdapterViews.get_cursor_px()`; the lint carries an allow-list of the Adapter's registered files. (Earlier text:) Either the Adapter hands the cursor position and zoom edges to the pipeline root, or the lint carries an allow-list naming the pipeline root."
  },
  {
   "id": "C128",
   "adr": "ADR-0018",
   "where": "design/gdd/player-controller-input.md",
   "old": "every written value has zero fractional part; the `Light2D.rotation` may be fractional.",
   "new": "every written value has zero fractional part, except the beam `Light2D` position, which is the floored cell plus `CELL_CENTRE` written through `Placement.put_light_origin` (ADR-0018 section 3); the `Light2D.rotation` may be fractional."
  }
 ],
